meta {
  name: 03-authorization
  seq: 4
}

docs {
  Every access-control guarantee, in one place a reviewer can read end to end.

  CONVENTIONS.md describes authorization as two independent levels: a coarse
  permission on the endpoint, AND an object-level ownership check in the
  service. Enforcing only the first is an IDOR bug. Both levels are exercised
  here — the permission level by the unauthenticated and non-admin requests, the
  object level by `other` attempting to act on `owner`'s item.

  This folder creates its own item so it never depends on whether folder 02 ran
  or left one behind.
}
